      "fix/kill-leftover-emerald: the black+gold rebrand finally reaches the last green. --apex-accent was still 160 84% 36% (light) / 160 84% 45% (dark) — emerald, carried over from before the 2026-08-02 green→gold pass and flagged as explicitly NOT done in the perf/site-wide-optimization receipt. It drives RecruitFAQ (the open question's index pill, chevron and border), GlobalSidebar hover, and --apex-hover-ring, so the landing FAQ and the sidebar were quietly still green. Both theme blocks retargeted to the gold that already exists — hue/sat identical to --apex-gold / --primary / --ring (45 85% 52%, src/index.css:85) and to the emerald→gold Tailwind ramp remap — rather than a fourth invented shade. The far bigger find came from actually screenshotting the rendered page instead of grepping src/: the Login \"Sign In\" button was still BRIGHT EMERALD with a green halo. tailwind.config.ts defined bg-apex-gradient and shadow-apex-glow as literal hsl(168 84% 42%) → hsl(160 84% 39%), and literal hsl in the config is not reachable by the emerald→gold palette remap that fixed ~1,850 utilities. Those two utilities are the entire visual identity of the shared GradientButton primitive, used by 19 surfaces including Login, HireLink, AgentSignup, GetLicensed, ApplicantCheckin, SeminarPage, TrainingIndex, PendingApproval and the /apply success page — so the primary CTA on the applicant-facing funnel had been green this whole time. Fixed in BOTH tailwind configs, because the landing config is a separate build and touching only one ships a half-green site — the documented failure mode from the 2026-08-02 pass.",
    detail:
      "Contrast was treated as the hard constraint, not an afterthought, because --apex-accent renders as TEXT (RecruitFAQ chevron + hover, GlobalSidebar hover) and as a fill behind --apex-bg ink (the FAQ index pill) — the same shape as the recently-shipped mobile-CTA bug that painted near-black ink on a near-black fill. Gold at 52% lightness on a white card is 1.8:1, so the LIGHT block deliberately does NOT take the canonical 52%: it is 45 85% 28%, measured in the browser at 5.4:1 for accent-as-text on --apex-card and 4.81:1 for pill-ink-on-pill-fill — both clear WCAG AA, where the emerald it replaced was 3.0:1 and 2.7:1 and had never passed either. The DARK block (what the app actually force-locks — index.html sets class=\"dark\") keeps the canonical 45 85% 52%, measured at 9.6:1 accent-text-on-card and 10.49:1 for the gold-fill/dark-ink pill. Sign In button measured after the fix: linear-gradient(135deg, rgb(237,185,29), rgb(221,145,14)) with rgb(27,22,14) ink at 9.9:1, gold glow. Every number above was read out of getComputedStyle in headless Chrome against the local production build, not calculated on paper. FILES: src/styles/apex-tokens.css (both :root and :root.dark accent/accent-soft/accent-strong). tailwind.config.ts + tailwind.config.landing.cjs (apex-gradient, apex-gradient-soft, apex-glow, apex-glow-strong — kept byte-identical between the two). src/index.css — .light .text-teal-*/.text-emerald-* were forcing those utilities BACK to real teal/emerald with !important, undoing the palette remap (now the same dark gold, 5.4:1); the border-emerald button hover glow routed to --primary. Component sweep, 13 sites in AgentCommandDashboard (Recharts strokes/fills/gradient stops + a tooltip border and label colour) and 1 in BookReconciliation routed to hsl(var(--primary)); ScrollProgress's teal→purple→amber rainbow (the last three-hue gradient, previously flagged) collapsed to a gold ramp; AuroraBackground's teal radial, gameFx's \"emerald\" screen-flash, and the Login + ResetPassword drop-shadow glows all moved to --primary; the CallCenterProgressRing and the two canvas waveform recorders (InterviewRecorder + CallCenterVoiceRecorder, which cannot read CSS vars so carry literal gold). Semantic green was deliberately left alone everywhere — the CallCenterProgressRing completeGradient stays green (only its teal end-stop moved), BookReconciliation's unsupported slice stays red, and .light .text-green-* is untouched, for the same reason tailwind.config.ts remaps emerald/teal but not green. VERIFIED: a repo-wide sweep for hsl(145-179 …) across src + both tailwind configs + index.html + public returns zero live values (only comments naming what was removed), and a runtime scan of every loaded stylesheet on the built page returns 2 remaining rules, both of them the sonner toast library's own --success-bg. Screenshots at 390x844 against the local prod build: landing/RecruitFAQ open state and /login. NOT screenshotted: the sidebar and a dashboard page — both sit behind ProtectedRoute and no supabase service key exists on this machine to mint an admin session, so they are covered instead by computed-style receipts of the exact utilities they use (.text-apex-accent = rgb(237,185,29) at 9.6:1 on .bg-apex-card, --apex-hover-ring = hsl(45 85% 52% / .4)). tsc ratchet 233/233, zero new errors; build green; no surface deleted.",
