    label:
      "fix/manager-deal-insert: /dashboard/bulk-deals is ProtectedRoute requireAdmin allowManagers — managers are deliberately let onto the page — but public.deals had no manager INSERT policy. It carried deals_admin_all (ALL), deals_own_insert / deals_own_read / deals_own_update (own agent row only) and deals_manager_read_downline (SELECT). A manager could therefore READ their whole downline's deals and INSERT none of them: every pasted row that wasn't their own personal production came back 42501. The page invited them in and then refused the one thing it exists to do. Fixed with deals_manager_insert_downline, whose WITH CHECK is the character-for-character twin of the existing read policy's USING clause — same my_downline_agent_ids() call, not a freshly-invented hierarchy expression — so read scope and write scope can no longer drift apart when the hierarchy logic changes. Scope is not widened: a manager still cannot insert outside their downline, and a plain agent still cannot insert for anyone but themselves. INSERT only — BulkDeals performs exactly one write and no UPDATE, so deals_own_update was left alone. Second, deeper bug found while verifying: deals.client_phone and deals.client_dob are NOT NULL with no default, and the BulkDeals row object never supplied either, so every paste from that page failed with 23502 for ADMINS too. The RLS fix on its own would have shipped a page that still could not insert a single row — a green policy over a dead surface.",
    detail:
      "DB (applied via bot-sql, read back from pg_policies): CREATE POLICY deals_manager_insert_downline ON public.deals FOR INSERT TO authenticated WITH CHECK (has_role((SELECT auth.uid()), 'manager') AND agent_id IN (SELECT agent_id FROM my_downline_agent_ids())). Verified under SET LOCAL ROLE authenticated with real request.jwt.claims inside BEGIN … ROLLBACK, against two real live users. Manager KJ Vaughn (user 75b17131, 16 downline agents, confirmed has_role manager true / admin false): downline agent DENIED 42501 → ALLOWED, own agent row ALLOWED both before and after (deals_own_insert already covered it), outside downline DENIED 42501 before and after. Plain agent Jake Wantroba (no admin, no manager role): another agent DENIED, own row ALLOWED, outside downline DENIED — proof the policy grants nothing to non-managers. deals row count 1744 before and after, zero rows matching the probe policy_number survived, so none of the 16 AFTER INSERT triggers on public.deals (trg_deal_broadcast, trg_deal_celebration, trg_deal_closed_discord, trg_hot_streak, trg_deals_autopush_insuracloud …) fired for real. The BEFORE probe is what surfaced the 23502: the own-agent insert sailed past RLS and died on client_phone instead. src/pages/BulkDeals.tsx now sends client_phone: \"\" and client_dob: \"1900-01-01\" — the exact 'not captured' sentinels already carried by the 114 rows of the 2026-06-16 bulk import (all 114 inserted in a 5-second window, phone='' and dob=1900-01-01, done in raw SQL outside the app), not fabricated contact data. The paste format (client / carrier / product / policy line / agent name) carries no phone or DOB at all, so there is nothing real to fill in; same reasoning as the face_amount: 0 line directly below it. Implication worth stating plainly: this page has never successfully inserted a row through the UI. tsc ratchet 233/233, zero new errors; build green.",
