    label: "first-touch attribution: ad clicks stop evaporating on the way to /apply. 776 of 783 applications in production (99.1%) had utm_source = NULL, and gclid had never been captured anywhere in the codebase — not once, in any file. The cause was structural, not a broken pixel: Apply.tsx read every attribution field with searchParams.get(...) at SUBMIT time, and nothing persisted them. A visitor landing on /?utm_source=google&gclid=Cj0... and clicking 'Start My Application' moves to /apply on a client-side route change that carries no query string, so by the time the form posted the params were already gone. Only the 7 people who hit /apply?utm_* directly ever recorded a source. Two things that cost money followed: ad spend could not be tied to applications, so channel ROI was guesswork; and with zero gclid stored, Google Ads offline conversion import — the mechanism for telling Google which clicks became real applicants — was flatly impossible. New src/lib/attribution.ts captures the landing signals at app entry (main.tsx, before React mounts) into localStorage as a write-once FIRST touch plus a sessionStorage LAST touch, and Apply.tsx now reads that instead of the URL. Same shape as the refSlug.ts relay that already fixed this for ?ref=.",
    detail: "NEW src/lib/attribution.ts: captureAttribution() reads utm_source/medium/campaign/term/content + gclid/gbraid/wbraid/fbclid/ttclid/msclkid + source from the landing URL, plus document.referrer and the landing path. First-touch writes to localStorage['apex_attr_first'] exactly once and is NEVER overwritten (that click earned the lead); last-touch overwrites sessionStorage['apex_attr_last'] whenever fresh signals appear. getAttribution() merges first → last → live URL, so a direct /apply?utm_* link still works when storage is unavailable. Hardening: every storage access is guarded with a memory-mirror fallback (Safari private mode / disabled storage / quota — jsdom 26 in our own test env exposes NO localStorage at all, which the suite now covers); values over 200 chars are dropped and the serialized payload is capped at 4 KB so a crafted query string cannot fill storage; the referrer is reduced to origin + pathname so a referring page's own query string can never smuggle PII in. src/main.tsx: captureAttribution() is the first call in the entry file, ahead of initWebVitals/bootAnalytics. src/pages/Apply.tsx: getTrafficPayload() and savePartialApplication() both switched from searchParams.get(...) to getAttribution(), and now send gclid/gbraid/wbraid/fbclid/ttclid/msclkid/firstTouchAt/firstLandingUrl/firstReferrer/attributionJson alongside the existing utm_* fields — form shape, validation, and submit flow otherwise untouched. supabase/functions/submit-application/index.ts: shared FirstTouchAttributionShape spread into BOTH the full-submit and quick-qualify zod schemas (all fields optional so a browser running a cached pre-ship bundle keeps submitting — verified against zod v3.22.4); firstTouchColumns() maps them onto the applications columns and drops a non-ISO firstTouchAt rather than risking a 22007 on the whole insert; stripNullFirstTouch() guards the two UPDATE paths (quick-qualify re-submit, quick→full upgrade) so a submit that carries no attribution cannot erase a gclid an earlier submit already stored — first-touch is write-once in the DB too. DB columns (gclid, gbraid, wbraid, fbclid, ttclid, msclkid, first_touch_at, first_landing_url, first_referrer, attribution_json + partial indexes) were migrated ahead of this ship and are confirmed present. NEW src/tests/lib/attribution.test.ts: 21 tests — first-touch survives the exact param-less SPA navigation that caused the bug, first-touch is never overwritten while last-touch does update, all six click ids captured, direct visits store nothing, external referrer counts as signal but same-origin does not, referrer query string stripped, oversized values dropped, and four storage-failure paths (setItem throws / getItem throws / storage entirely absent / malformed stored JSON) all prove no crash. Verified: npx tsc --noEmit 0 errors, tsc-error-count 233/233, check:empty-catch src 0/0, deno check on the edge function clean, 21/21 tests pass.",
    commit: "fix/first-touch-attribution",
