    label: "wave-31 blocking-modal 16 → 0 FULL PAY-DOWN SHIPPED — check-blocking-modal.mjs baseline dropped 16 → 0 in one wave by migrating every remaining native window.confirm() / bare confirm() callsite to `await askConfirm({...})` backed by a new promise-based useConfirm hook (src/hooks/useConfirm.tsx) wrapping Radix AlertDialog + a ConfirmProvider mounted inside src/components/layout/AuthenticatedShell.tsx so every dashboard route inherits it. Sites paid down (16 sites across 12 files): src/components/dashboard/AgentProfileDrawer.tsx L523/L549/L1000 (mark unlicensed + mark licensed + restore-deactivated), src/components/dashboard/ControlTerminal.tsx L205 (mutating-SQL guard with a formatted <pre> preview of the first 400 chars instead of a raw \\n\\n concat that mangled newlines on iOS), src/pages/AdminEmailGaps.tsx L106 (bulk re-queue course + Discord emails), src/pages/ContentLibrary.tsx L422/L434 (single delete + bulk-delete duplicates), src/pages/DashboardCRM.tsx L810/L833 (bulk portal-login send + bulk deactivate — both destructive), src/pages/HiringManagerAssignments.tsx L159 (remove-from-scope), src/pages/InactiveAgents.tsx L258 (bulk resolve status), src/pages/InboxPage.tsx L397 (bulk-delete notification + email logs), src/pages/admin/InviteLinks.tsx L175 (revoke invite link), src/pages/admin/SamHQ.tsx L214 (delete HQ task, converted from same-line if(confirm(...)) ternary to an async onClick that awaits askConfirm), src/pages/admin/TelegramBot.tsx L595 (queue broadcast), src/pages/admin/UnclaimedLeads.tsx L172 (reassign all filtered apps to Sam). Why this ships now: native window.confirm on Sam's daily-driver iPhone Safari freezes the main thread mid-paint, disables the address bar, refuses keyboard input unless the viewport scrolls to the tap origin, and can silently return undefined (which coerces to false) if a browser extension has swallowed the global — a whole failure class that fake-succeeds like the 465 InsuraCloud + 198 AgentLink rows the Operating Contract §NO-FAKE-SUCCESS calls out. All 16 replacements pipe through a single dialog whose destructive callsites now render tone='danger' (rose CTA) and non-destructive callsites default to the primary tone — so mass-delete UX visually differs from mass-send UX for the first time. Hook returns a promise resolved by the AlertDialogAction click or the AlertDialog's onOpenChange(false) fallback (Escape / overlay tap on iOS both close the sheet), with a resolvedRef guard so a race between the two paths can't double-resolve. scripts/check-blocking-modal.mjs BASELINE 16 → 0 locks the new floor forever; any future `window.confirm` / bare `confirm(` / `alert(` / `prompt(` in src/**/*.{tsx,ts,jsx,js} now fails at pre-commit unless explicitly annotated with `blocking-modal-allow:<reason>`. Naming the hook return `askConfirm` (not `confirm`) sidesteps the guard's regex-boundary check so `await askConfirm(` never trips the detector. Sixteenth surface audit since wave-4; thirteenth consecutive class-of-fix compounding asset since wave-16; first ratchet in the 11-class ladder (internal-nav / external-link / raw-db-slug / console-in-prod / empty-catch / debugger / blocking-modal / raw-SQL / @ts-ignore / hex-in-JSX-style / stale-key-in-list) to drop a non-zero baseline all the way to 0 in a single wave. Mobile-Safari-friendly, brand-locked (Radix AlertDialog inherits the shadcn theme, dark bg + gold accent per Brand Bible), keyboard-accessible (Tab/Enter/Escape all work), non-swallowable (the AlertDialog is a React-owned modal, not a browser primitive).",
